From 29e0b79795dff93125f7abc2fcce9203a9d4ec9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Tern <1263187-dt@users.noreply.gitlab.freedesktop.org>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 18:56:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bluez5: only clear BAP endpoints during BAP codec switching

A device can have both a configured A2DP transport and BAP transports.
The BAP switch planner correctly filters the selected endpoints by
codec, but its clear pass considers every unselected endpoint with a
transport. This can add a classic A2DP SEP to the BAP clear plan.

BlueZ's remote A2DP SEPs do not implement ClearConfiguration. The call
fails with UnknownMethod and aborts the switch before the selected BAP
endpoints are reconfigured.

Only consider BAP transports when finding endpoints to clear. Keep
clearing unselected BAP endpoints, including the source when changing
from duplex to playback, and leave the A2DP switching path unchanged.
---
 spa/plugins/bluez5/bluez5-dbus.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/spa/plugins/bluez5/bluez5-dbus.c b/spa/plugins/bluez5/bluez5-dbus.c
index f7eb46601..293a52a7d 100644
--- a/spa/plugins/bluez5/bluez5-dbus.c
+++ b/spa/plugins/bluez5/bluez5-dbus.c
@@ -5257,6 +5257,8 @@ int spa_bt_device_ensure_media_codec(struct spa_bt_device *device, const struct
 			bool active_ep = false;
 
 			spa_list_for_each(t, &device->transport_list, device_link) {
+				if (!(t->profile & SPA_BT_PROFILE_BAP_AUDIO))
+					continue;
 				if (spa_streq(t->remote_endpoint_path, sw->paths[i].path)) {
 					active_ep = true;
 					break;
